        "label": "Keep every Elestio computer's firewall equal to its computer row, every fifteen minutes",
        "job": "Read every computer row whose runs.firewall is kept at Elestio and make each Elestio firewall equal its rules, on a timer, so a port someone opens from the dashboard (Tail Logs and the like) is closed again by the next run and the rows alone say what is open.",
        "description": "Reads the person's computer rows (the held connection credential_name on descriptor 3: select name, runs.firewall from computer where runs.firewall.provider is elestio), signs in to Elestio once per account with the vault's elestio-api-key (descriptor 4, bound only to api.elest.io), and for each row runs what tool:keep-an-elestio-firewall does: reads the firewall, sends the row's whole rule set when it is off or differs (enableFirewall or updateFirewall) and reads it back. A rule set that leaves out 22/tcp or 4242/udp open to everyone is refused for that row. One row that fails is told and the others are still kept. apply false only reads. only names one row. Its wake keep-every-fifteen-minutes runs it every fifteen minutes on the computer whose vault holds both keys, switched on there with the connection's name as the switch input. Returns ok (every row ok), read_at (when the rows were read) and kept: per computer ok, action (null when it already matched), opened, closed, reason or error. Never the token, the session or the connection.",
